<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>NOAA has logged 841 hail reports in Dallas County since 1955, and 250 of them were golf ball size (1.75") or larger. April and May are the peak months, with a smaller second season in October.</li>
<li>Hail damage on composition shingles is often invisible from the street. Bruised mats, lost granules, and broken seal strips can turn into leaks months later.</li>
<li>Photograph the roof, gutters, vents, siding, and AC unit soon after the storm, and keep every receipt for tarping or emergency repairs.</li>
<li>Know your wind/hail deductible and whether your roof is covered at replacement cost or actual cash value before you read the estimate.</li>
